h(2, id: "includes") { 15. Includes }

p { Splice another .du file into the current document. Two spellings: }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
include "path/to/file.du"
include("path/to/file.du")
!}

p { The path is relative to the file that contains the statement, not to the process working directory. }

p { Resolution: }

list(ordered: true) {
  item { Join the path to the parent file's directory. }
  item { Canonicalize. Failure is an error on the include statement. }
  item { Reject the path if it is already on the current include stack (cycle). }
  item { Read, lex, parse the child. }
  item { Resolve includes inside the child. }
  item { Append the child's blocks to the parent. Child meta is discarded.fn(include-meta) }
  item { Pop the child from the stack so the same file may be included from a different branch. }
}

p { An empty path is a semantic error if the statement survives until analysis. A missing file fails earlier, during resolution. }

p { Watch mode adds every successfully resolved include to the watch set. }

p { This document is one HTML file built from several .du files. index.du holds meta, the banner, the title, the toc, the includes, and the footnote definitions. }
